## How It Works

| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Outer loop** | Runs `n-1` times; each pass places the next largest element in its correct position |
| **Inner loop** | Compares adjacent elements and swaps them if they're in the wrong order |
| **Optimization** | The `swapped` flag detects if the array is already sorted, allowing early exit |

## Complexity

| Case | Time Complexity |
|------|----------------|
| **Best** (already sorted) | O(n) — with the `swapped` optimization |
| **Average** | O(n²) |
| **Worst** (reverse sorted) | O(n²) |
| **Space** | O(1) — in-place sorting |

